1
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:42,442
Good morning.

2
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:45,229
Good morning. My name is Richard Stewart.

3
00:00:45,229 --> 00:00:46,909
I'm here to see Mr. Carlson.

4
00:00:46,909 --> 00:00:50,625
Please  sit down,Mr.Stewart.  Mr. Carlson will be with you shortly.

5
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:53,603
Thank you.

6
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:56,003
Excuse me, Mr. Carlson,

7
00:00:56,003 --> 00:00:57,570
but Richard Stewart is here

8
00:00:57,570 --> 00:00:59,559
for his ten o'clock appointment with you.

9
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,559
OK. Thank you.

10
00:01:01,559 --> 00:01:04,537
Like I said, he'll be with you shortly.

11
00:01:04,537 --> 00:01:08,493
Thank you.

12
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:14,449
Yes, Mr. Carlson. Yes, sir.

13
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,427
He's ready for you, Mr. Stewart.

14
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:19,427
Thank you. In there?

15
00:01:19,427 --> 00:01:26,361
Yes. In there. Good luck.

16
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:29,339
Come in, come in.

17
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:32,984
This is a crazy morning. Hello, Richard.

18
00:01:32,984 --> 00:01:33,650
Hello, Mr. Carlson.

19
00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:35,295
Sit down, sit down.

20
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:39,304
Thank you for seeing me on such short notice.

21
00:01:39,304 --> 00:01:41,251
I hope you've brought your pictures along.

22
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:47,207
I see that you have. Let's get right to it.

23
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:49,463
We need a new coffee-table book,

24
00:01:49,463 --> 00:01:53,963
and a book of photos about the United States still feels right.

25
00:01:53,963 --> 00:02:06,074
OK, let's take a look.

26
00:02:06,074 --> 00:02:17,855
Good. Very good. Family Album, U.S.A.

27
00:02:17,855 --> 00:02:19,592
It's an excellent title.

28
00:02:19,592 --> 00:02:22,244
If you had to describe the book in one sentence,

29
00:02:22,244 --> 00:02:22,942
how would you do it?

30
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:28,898
Well, I'd describe it as a book which is a ...

31
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:31,876
a portrait of the United States--

32
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:36,123
the places, the people--mostly the people.

33
00:02:36,123 --> 00:02:39,016
The things they do, the ways they live,

34
00:02:39,016 --> 00:02:41,810
the places they visit, and the landmarks.

35
00:02:41,810 --> 00:02:45,018
A photographic journey.

36
00:02:45,018 --> 00:02:46,766
These are wonderful--

37
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:49,744
these photos in your performing arts section.

38
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,887
Carnegie Hall, Lincoln Center.

39
00:02:51,887 --> 00:02:54,222
I'm glad you like them.

40
00:02:54,222 --> 00:02:55,700
I do, but ...

41
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:58,678
But?

42
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:03,656
There's something missing. You've got a good eye, Richard.

43
00:03:03,656 --> 00:03:05,786
You're a terrific photographer.

44
00:03:05,786 --> 00:03:09,052
But before I can publish your work,

45
00:03:09,052 --> 00:03:11,209
I need to meet with my marketing department,

46
00:03:11,209 --> 00:03:14,380
and you've got to do one more thing.

47
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:16,545
What's that, Mr. Carlson?

48
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:18,688
In the section on culture,

49
00:03:18,688 --> 00:03:20,483
you've included performing arts centers,

50
00:03:20,483 --> 00:03:25,479
but you've left out street performance. The mimes.

51
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:30,457
The musicians. The dancers--in the parks and on the streets.

52
00:03:30,457 --> 00:03:32,799
Richard, if you go out    Richard,

53
00:03:32,799 --> 00:03:35,080
and photograph street performances in the city,

54
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:37,791
you'll have it.

55
00:03:37,791 --> 00:03:40,712
That is a great idea.

56
00:03:40,712 --> 00:03:44,014
The performing arts centers and the street performances.

57
00:03:44,014 --> 00:03:45,014
I'll do it.

58
00:03:45,014 --> 00:03:48,825
If you do it, I'll publish your work.

59
00:03:48,825 --> 00:03:49,303
Are you serious?

60
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:51,303
I've never been more serious.

61
00:03:51,303 --> 00:03:55,259
When do you think you can return with street performances?

62
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:58,237
A couple of weeks.

63
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:01,215
If they're as good as the rest of these pictures, it's a deal.

64
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:07,171
You won't be disappointed, Mr. Carlson. Thanks.

65
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:12,374
Good-bye, Richard, and good luck. See you in two weeks.

66
00:04:12,374 --> 00:04:16,105
Good-bye, Mr. Carlson. Thanks.

67
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:22,060
So if you like the street-performance photos,

68
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:26,101
you'll really publish Family Album, U.S.A.?

69
00:04:26,101 --> 00:05:36,829
When I say something, I mean it.

70
00:05:36,829 --> 00:06:13,245
Go to work. Good-bye.

71
00:06:13,245 --> 00:06:16,245
Good-bye.
